A||N||6||FieroSTETZ||archie, ever do swaps on other cars?||||5||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||08-24-2000||11:20 PM||||hey archie, do you/have you ever done engine swaps on other cars? just curious! i recently got my butt chewed by a geo metro (mostly was surprised he tried to race, but that thing moved) i talked to the guy later(he pulled into mcdonalds lot), its a metro with the engine/fuel system/drive train from a geo storm. also has extensive engine work done, says it puts about 150 to the ground (good god, in a metro!) i was just thinking about what other cars would be fun to do engine swaps in... viper v10 into a dodge dakota  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Archie||08-25-2000||01:34 AM||||In the years BF (Before Fiero) I used to do V-8 swaps to just about everything I could get my hands on. I put V-8 Chevy engines into an XKE, Bug Eyed Sprite, Opel GT, TR Spitfire and more, you can read about it at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/about.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/about.htm</A> <P>For the last 14+ years, I have done nothing but Fieros. I only work on "non-stock" (V-8 only) Fieros and have never even changed spark plugs on a stock Fiero. We also do some body stuff like the Fino & Finale. As far as engine swaps, I only do V-8 swaps to Fieros. I don't do 3.1's, 3.4's, 3.8's or NStars. I know I could make a few extra $ if I would do the little V-6 swaps but I am 100% commited to SBC's in Fieros and I feel like I'd be a traitor if I did a car for a customer that I wouldn't drive, thus I do none of the "other" swaps. <P>Thanks For asking.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||08-25-2000||07:56 PM||||  I'm going to install a 3.0l Taurus SHO V6 with the 5 speed into my 94 Topaz.  I've got the planning all done up.  And I've already intalled front and rear 3/4" stabilizer bars and 16" wheels with 215/50vr16 rubber.  Just one more sleeper for you to watch out for!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As for the guy in the Metro, how does he even get anyone to race him?||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||08-25-2000||08:20 PM||||he has a few stickers across the back "your girlfriend likes me" "drive fast die young- honda, etc" license plates read "this geo eats chevies and shits fords" and other such inspirational things. i would imagine its not much of a top end car (scary!) but oughta be pretty quick light to light?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||08-25-2000||08:44 PM||||LOL Olympic, yep, that will be one hell of a sleeper. A couple of guys I knew at the Muskoday indian reserve did that swap a couple of years ago. It was pretty funny to see. I was riding back with my brother in his Civic and this little white POS tempo flies past us with about 7 or 8 natives in it (no kidding)and we tried to catch up to them but couldn't. We saw them later at the gas station in town and talked to the guy, and he took an SHO out of an eighties Taurus and dropped it in. Anyways, you guys will have to race each other sometime!||||reg||1
